[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="BuffStatusImmunity" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://cm107udeeibkt" path="res://engine/character/buff/archtypes/buff_status_immunity.gd" id="1_immunity"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_immunity")
; "all adjacent allies gain immunity to Impaired". The vanilla archetype does the whole job:
; BuffStatusImmunity.check_if_passive_applies (buff_status_immunity.gd:8-9) answers the engine's
; immunity query, and on_application (:11-13) CLEARS any matching status the ally already has, so an
; Impaired ally walking into the cloud is cleaned up rather than merely protected from the next one.
;
; TWO DIFFERENT MECHANISMS REACH THE SAME PLACE, and a spec should know which it is testing:
;   - an ordinary Impaired (a StatusCondition in unit.state.statuses) is CLEARED on application by
;     the line above;
;   - an Impaired supplied by some OTHER buff's applies_statuses is not in that array and so is not
;     cleared - it is instead SUPPRESSED, because get_current_statuses (unit_condition.gd:379-382)
;     checks has_gained_immunity_to_status before folding it in.
; Both leave the ally un-Impaired, which is what the card asks. Task 3's spec tests both paths.
;
; Vanilla precedent, same archetype on the same kind of aura: the Drake's
; content/frames/ipsn/mf_drake/cp_fortress_protocol/buff_fortress_immunity.tres.
immune_to_statuses = Array[StringName]([&"impaired"])
to = &"status_immunity"
; DELIBERATELY VISIBLE, and this is where we diverge from the Drake. buff_fortress_immunity sets
; hide_from_player = true because Fortress applies three buffs at once and would otherwise wear three
; chips. Here the immunity is one of the two things the card promises an ally, and the ally has no
; other signal that standing next to the Myconid is doing anything - so it wears a chip and
; test_content_integrity.gd's VISIBLE_BUFFS lists it. The SP3 icon pass owes it an icon, and may
; reuse vanilla's Fortress immunity art (author's call at the contact sheet).
;
; `until` stays at MANUAL for the reason buff_fungal_network_spores.tres gives at length: the AURA
; owns the lifetime of everything it applies.
